{
  "name": "310. Groq transcription from an audio URL with duration usage (groq transcription url)",
  "description": "Groq takes an audio URL in the \"url\" form field in place of the file (contract C4). The native /v1/audio/transcriptions route accepts url without file and leaves the provider to decide: Groq forwards the URL unchanged as a form field with no file part (Bifrost never downloads it); a provider that takes only a file answers 400 caller_unsupported_parameter with error.param \"url\", refused before a key is chosen so no upstream call is made. Groq's verbose_json reports the audio length as \"duration\" and no usage; Bifrost reports that duration as usage {type: duration, seconds} (contract C5), the same for every OpenAI-compatible host, and keeps a vendor's own usage as sent. Groq's 10-second minimum is the caller's price rule and is not applied here. The URL is this fixture's public copy on the upstream repository, pinned to a commit. The /openai drop-in route still requires a file, so it takes no URL-only request; it reaches the duration-usage backfill, pinned by its own case.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "/v1/audio/transcriptions - url without file reaches Groq on the named key, duration becomes usage - groq/whisper-large-v3-turbo",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('url-only transcription returns text and duration usage', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql(200);",
              "  var j = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(j.text, 'empty text: ' + pm.response.text()).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
              "  pm.expect(j.duration, 'verbose_json duration missing: ' + pm.response.text()).to.be.above(0);",
              "  pm.expect(j.usage && j.usage.type, 'usage type: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql('duration');",
              "  pm.expect(j.usage.seconds, 'usage seconds must be the vendor duration: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql(j.duration);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('one attempt on the named Groq key', function () {",
              "  var ef = pm.response.json().extra_fields || {};",
              "  var ri = ef.routing_info || {};",
              "  pm.expect(ef.provider, 'served by: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql('groq');",
              "  pm.expect(ri.key, 'the caller named this key: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql('Groq API Key');",
              "  pm.expect(!!ri.is_fallback, 'no fallback may run: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql(false);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "x-bf-api-key",
            "value": "Groq API Key"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "formdata",
          "formdata": [
            {
              "key": "model",
              "value": "groq/whisper-large-v3-turbo",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "key": "url",
              "value": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/maximhq/bifrost/1e14ce7e5c9e51f9496d1897c5b12daacac8791f/tests/e2e/api/fixtures/sample.mp3",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "key": "response_format",
              "value": "verbose_json",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/audio/transcriptions",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "audio",
            "transcriptions"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
